1
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:10,780
Smell that?

2
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:13,950
That's the smell of new comic books.

3
00:00:14,010 --> 00:00:17,110
Oh, yes.

4
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:20,180
They're on me today, boys.

5
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:21,710
You're paying?

6
00:00:21,780 --> 00:00:24,350
Have you been selling your sperm again?

7
00:00:24,410 --> 00:00:26,650
No, I'm celebrating.

8
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:28,710
As we speak, the space shuttle

9
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:30,550
Is docking at the at the international space station

10
00:00:30,610 --> 00:00:32,650
Where it will deploy the wolowitz zero-gravity

11
00:00:32,710 --> 00:00:35,210
Waste disposal system.

12
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:36,610
Oh, get over yourself.

13
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:38,250
It's a high-tech toilet.

14
00:00:38,310 --> 00:00:40,010
Just think.

15
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:41,710
Thanks to your hard work,

16
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:43,350
An international crew of astronauts

17
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:47,010
Will "boldly go where no man has gone before."

18
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:48,480
Is that supposed to be funny?

19
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:50,110
I believe it is.

20
00:00:50,180 --> 00:00:51,710
The combination of the star trek reference

21
00:00:51,780 --> 00:00:53,550
And the play on words involving the double-meaning

22
00:00:53,610 --> 00:00:54,810
Of the verb "to go"

23
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:56,210
Suggests that leonard is humorously mocking

24
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:57,610
Your efforts in space plumbing.

25
00:00:58,910 --> 00:01:00,910
Okay, make your little jokes,

26
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:03,180
But of the four of us, I'm the only one making

27
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:06,450
Any real-world contribution to science and technology.

28
00:01:06,510 --> 00:01:09,010
He's right. this is an important achievement, for two reasons.

29
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:10,750
Number one...

30
00:01:10,810 --> 00:01:12,850
And, of course, number two!

31
00:01:14,410 --> 00:01:16,510
Oh, clever!

32
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:18,310
Playing on the use of cardinal numbers

33
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:20,410
As euphemisms for bodily functions.

34
00:01:24,910 --> 00:01:27,610
Here, sheldon, I pulled the new hellboy for you.

35
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:29,180
It's mind-blowing.

36
00:01:29,250 --> 00:01:32,480
Excuse me. spoiler alert.

37
00:01:32,550 --> 00:01:34,850
I didn't spoil anything.

38
00:01:34,910 --> 00:01:36,580
You told me it's mind-blowing.

39
00:01:36,650 --> 00:01:38,550
So, my mind is going into it pre-blown.

40
00:01:38,610 --> 00:01:42,280
And once a mind is pre-blown, it cannot be re-blown.

41
00:01:42,350 --> 00:01:43,710
I'm sorry.

42
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:46,010
Said the grinch to christmas.

43
00:01:48,950 --> 00:01:50,050
Uh, hey, leonard.

44
00:01:50,110 --> 00:01:51,410
Could I talk to you about something?

45
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:52,210
Sure, what's up?

46
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:53,480
Remember I went out with

47
00:01:53,550 --> 00:01:54,910
Your friend, penny, a couple weeks ago?

48
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:56,310
Yeah, vaguely.

49
00:01:56,380 --> 00:01:57,550
Sure you remember.

50
00:01:57,610 --> 00:01:59,550
That was the night you went to the bar and made a fool

51
00:01:59,610 --> 00:02:02,150
Of yourself trying to pick up strange women.

52
00:02:04,510 --> 00:02:06,450
What about it?

53
00:02:06,510 --> 00:02:10,080
Well, uh, the thing is, the date didn't go that well.

54
00:02:10,150 --> 00:02:12,410
Oh. too bad.

55
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:16,250
I guess the thing to do now is just pick yourself up,

56
00:02:16,310 --> 00:02:18,250
Dust yourself off, forget it and move on.

57
00:02:18,310 --> 00:02:19,150
I can't do that.

58
00:02:19,210 --> 00:02:21,680
Why the hell not?

59
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:24,110
'cause we're going out again tomorrow.

60
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:25,510
Excuse me, stuart.

61
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:26,750
Have you read the new flash?

62
00:02:26,810 --> 00:02:28,110
- No. - well, I have

63
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:30,980
And it will knock your socks off!

64
00:02:31,050 --> 00:02:33,410
Good luck getting them back on.

65
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:37,910
Uh, anyway,

66
00:02:37,980 --> 00:02:40,010
I figure this is probably my last shot with penny

67
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:41,110
And I don't want to screw it up.

68
00:02:41,180 --> 00:02:43,250
Nobody wants that.

69
00:02:43,310 --> 00:02:45,450
Here's my question:it's the second date,

70
00:02:45,510 --> 00:02:50,310
You think she'll be expecting things to get physical?

71
00:02:51,950 --> 00:02:54,550
Uh, gee, um...

72
00:02:55,650 --> 00:02:58,610
My initial reaction is "no," but, um,

73
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:01,280
Let me think about it and get back to you, okay?

74
00:03:01,350 --> 00:03:03,010
Okay, so, you'll give me a call?

75
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:04,050
Yeah, or you call me.

76
00:03:04,110 --> 00:03:05,380
Great.

77
00:03:06,350 --> 00:03:08,210
Or nobody calls anyone.

78
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:10,580
Interesting.

79
00:03:10,650 --> 00:03:14,050
Penny's current suitor asking advice from her former suitor.

80
00:03:14,110 --> 00:03:17,250
You know, thanks for closed- captioning my pain, raj.

81
00:03:17,310 --> 00:03:20,010
Hey, want to make sure he gets nowhere with penny

82
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:22,610
Without jeopardizing your friendship with either of them?

83
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:24,210
I'm listening.

84
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:26,150
Just tell him to do everything

85
00:03:26,210 --> 00:03:28,480
You've done with her for the last two years.

86
00:03:59,070 --> 00:04:00,270
Hey, leonard.

87
00:04:00,330 --> 00:04:01,400
Oh, hi.

88
00:04:01,470 --> 00:04:02,930
- How's it going? - good, good.

89
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,030
- You? - fine.

90
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:07,000
Oh, hey, can I ask you something?

91
00:04:07,070 --> 00:04:07,900
Sure.

92
00:04:07,970 --> 00:04:09,670
You know your friend stuart?

93
00:04:09,730 --> 00:04:12,700
Yes.

94
00:04:12,770 --> 00:04:14,530
Well, he asked me out again and I said yes,

95
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:15,830
And then I started thinking

96
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:17,230
Maybe I should talk to you first.

97
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:18,470
About what?

98
00:04:18,530 --> 00:04:20,400
Well, does it bother you,

99
00:04:20,470 --> 00:04:22,400
Me going out with one of your friends?

100
00:04:22,470 --> 00:04:23,630
'cause you know, you and me...

101
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:27,070
No. no, that's the past.

102
00:04:27,130 --> 00:04:29,300
I'm really more of a "right now" kind of guy.

103
00:04:29,370 --> 00:04:31,200
You know, living in the moment.

104
00:04:31,270 --> 00:04:33,800
Although I do have to live a little in the future,

105
00:04:33,870 --> 00:04:35,370
'cause, well, that's my job.

106
00:04:35,430 --> 00:04:38,300
Of course, my fondness for classic science fiction

107
00:04:38,370 --> 00:04:40,200
Does draw my attention backwards,

108
00:04:40,270 --> 00:04:43,000
But those stories often take place in the future.

109
00:04:45,430 --> 00:04:47,470
In conclusion, no, it doesn't bother me.

110
00:04:49,470 --> 00:04:51,730
Okay, well, that's really cool of you.

111
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:53,430
Yeah, well, I wouldn't say cool.

112
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:55,000
I'd just say...

113
00:04:55,070 --> 00:04:57,230
"that's leonard!"

114
00:04:57,300 --> 00:05:00,070
Well, in that case, do you mind giving me some advice?

115
00:05:00,130 --> 00:05:01,770
About stuart?

116
00:05:01,830 --> 00:05:03,230
Love to.

117
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:05,000
He's very shy.

118
00:05:05,070 --> 00:05:07,230
How do I make him feel more comfortable around me?

119
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:09,000
Well, first of all, don't underestimate

120
00:05:09,070 --> 00:05:11,730
The value of discomfort.

121
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:13,230
- Really? - oh, yes.

122
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:14,930
Stuart thrives under pressure.

123
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,170
That's why he works in a comic book store.

124
00:05:23,250 --> 00:05:26,150
Oh, it's stuart.

125
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:31,650
You're not going to answer it?

126
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:34,420
He wants to talk about penny.

127
00:05:34,490 --> 00:05:35,820
I don't want to talk about penny.

128
00:05:35,890 --> 00:05:38,020
You're making an assumption.

129
00:05:39,390 --> 00:05:41,750
Perhaps the comic book store is on fire.

130
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:44,320
And he needs your assistance.

131
00:05:44,390 --> 00:05:47,190
Why would he call me?

132
00:05:47,250 --> 00:05:49,820
We don't know.

133
00:05:49,890 --> 00:05:52,550
And if you don't answer the phone, we can't know.

134
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:56,290
I'm not answering the phone, sheldon.

135
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:02,450
- Answer the phone, leonard. - no!

136
00:06:04,850 --> 00:06:06,990
There, it went to voice mail.

137
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:15,620
Aren't you going to check your messages?

138
00:06:18,020 --> 00:06:19,390
No.

139
00:06:19,450 --> 00:06:20,350
You have to check your messages, leonard!

140
00:06:20,350 --> 00:06:21,690
The in a

141
00:06:21,750 --> 00:06:23,450
Is one half of a social contract

142
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:26,190
Which is completed by the checking of the message.

143
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:28,650
If that contract breaks down,

144
00:06:28,720 --> 00:06:30,690
Then all social contracts break down

145
00:06:30,750 --> 00:06:33,050
And we descend into anarchy.

146
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:37,550
It must be hell inside your head.

147
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:41,450
At times.

148
00:06:42,590 --> 00:06:45,220
Guys, we have a code red.

149
00:06:45,290 --> 00:06:47,190
You mean "code red" the hospital emergency alert,

150
00:06:47,260 --> 00:06:49,120
"code red" the computer worm, or "code red" the cherry-flavored

151
00:06:49,190 --> 00:06:51,560
Soft drink from the makers of mountain dew?

152
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:53,860
Look, I was going over the schematics

153
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:56,660
On my zero-g toilet, and I made a teeny tiny mistake

154
00:06:56,720 --> 00:06:58,360
On the specifications for the diverter valve.

155
00:06:58,420 --> 00:07:00,390
How teeny tiny?

156
00:07:00,460 --> 00:07:02,460
It's gonna fail after about ten flushes.

157
00:07:03,590 --> 00:07:05,220
But the mission is for six months.

158
00:07:05,290 --> 00:07:06,420
Yeah, see, that's the code red.

159
00:07:06,490 --> 00:07:09,090
It's kind of like a jack-in-the-box.

160
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:11,260
No one knows exactly when, but at some point

161
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:14,020
Something way worse than a puppet is gonna pop out of that box.

162
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:17,760
Have you notified nasa?

163
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:19,460
No, are you crazy? what am I gonna say?

164
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:21,070
"i screwed up your toilet and pretty soon

165
00:07:21,070 --> 00:07:22,270
"there's gonna be crap floating

166
00:07:22,330 --> 00:07:23,700
All over your nice shiny space station"?

167
00:07:23,770 --> 00:07:26,300
So, what are you gonna do?

168
00:07:26,370 --> 00:07:28,300
I'm gonna figure out how to fix it, then I'll tell them.

169
00:07:28,370 --> 00:07:30,300
So, what do you need us for?

170
00:07:30,370 --> 00:07:32,600
He can't figure out how to fix it.

171
00:07:32,670 --> 00:07:34,870
Hey, you said you were gonna be supportive.

172
00:07:34,930 --> 00:07:36,300
I'm trying,

173
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:38,670
but you have to admit this is pretty damn funny.

174
00:07:39,630 --> 00:07:41,070
I agree.

175
00:07:41,130 --> 00:07:43,000
It's the juxtaposition of the high-tech nature

176
00:07:43,070 --> 00:07:46,030
Of space exploration against the banality of a malfunctioning toilet

177
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:47,670
That provides the comic fodder here.

178
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:54,070
Check your messages.

179
00:07:57,250 --> 00:07:59,480
All right, this is an exact duplicate

180
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:02,750
Of the wolowitz zero-gravity human waste disposal system

181
00:08:02,750 --> 00:08:04,750
As deployed on the international space station.

182
00:08:04,810 --> 00:08:09,210
Don't you mean the wolowitz zero-gravity human waste distribution system?

183
00:08:10,950 --> 00:08:14,110
Good one.

184
00:08:14,180 --> 00:08:16,380
Yeah, it's hilarious.

185
00:08:16,450 --> 00:08:17,980
Now...

186
00:08:18,050 --> 00:08:20,910
Here's an approximation of the spare parts

187
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:22,580
Available on the space station.

188
00:08:22,650 --> 00:08:24,810
We gotta find a way, using nothing but this,

189
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:26,310
To reinforce this so the waste material

190
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:27,650
Avoids the spinning turbine.

191
00:08:27,710 --> 00:08:31,210
You mean so it doesn't hit the fan?

192
00:08:34,150 --> 00:08:35,910
Yeah, I have to say,

193
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:39,150
I thought the toilet humor would get less funny with repetition.

194
00:08:39,210 --> 00:08:40,910
Apparently, there is no law

195
00:08:40,980 --> 00:08:43,610
Of diminishing comedic returns with space poop.

196
00:08:48,450 --> 00:08:50,050
- Hey, leonard. - hey, stuart.

197
00:08:50,110 --> 00:08:51,650
- You busy? - um...

198
00:08:51,710 --> 00:08:53,710
Classified, leonard.

199
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:56,680
Yeah, it's a regular manhattan project.

200
00:08:57,910 --> 00:08:58,850
What's up?

201
00:08:58,910 --> 00:09:01,050
Well, tonight's my date with penny

202
00:09:01,110 --> 00:09:03,010
And since we haven't been able to connect by phone...

203
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:04,550
Yeah, I'm sorry, it's been broken.

204
00:09:04,610 --> 00:09:06,410
- Or e-mail. - yeah, that's broken, too.

205
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:08,480
Everything's broken.

206
00:09:08,550 --> 00:09:11,050
Anyway, I was just wondering if you had any last-minute advice.

207
00:09:11,110 --> 00:09:15,980
Uh, all right, well, off the top of my head,

208
00:09:16,050 --> 00:09:17,750
You know, I think the most important thing with penny

209
00:09:17,810 --> 00:09:19,280
Is to go really slow.

210
00:09:20,350 --> 00:09:23,150
I mean, glacial.

211
00:09:23,210 --> 00:09:24,450
Okay.

212
00:09:24,510 --> 00:09:26,650
You know, guys come onto her all the time,

213
00:09:26,710 --> 00:09:29,280
So, you need to set yourself apart.

214
00:09:29,350 --> 00:09:31,080
You know, be a little shy,

215
00:09:31,150 --> 00:09:34,950
Don't make too much eye contact.

216
00:09:35,010 --> 00:09:37,750
And, you know, treat her with, like, cool detachment

217
00:09:37,810 --> 00:09:41,110
And-and, you know, fear.

218
00:09:41,180 --> 00:09:41,950
Fear?

219
00:09:42,010 --> 00:09:44,450
Yeah, like, uh,

220
00:09:44,510 --> 00:09:47,810
You're afraid that if you touch her, she'll break.

221
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:51,180
Well, that plays right into my wheelhouse.

222
00:09:51,250 --> 00:09:53,080
Good, good.

223
00:09:53,150 --> 00:09:54,650
Well, uh, you-you kids have fun tonight.

224
00:09:54,710 --> 00:09:56,410
- Thanks, leonard. - uh-huh.

225
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:58,110
What is that thing anyway?

226
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:00,650
You don't know what this is?

227
00:10:00,710 --> 00:10:02,850
- No. - good. get out.

228
00:10:06,250 --> 00:10:08,410
Be afraid of penny.

229
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:10,050
Nice. very crafty.

230
00:10:10,110 --> 00:10:12,050
It wasn't bad advice.

231
00:10:12,110 --> 00:10:15,280
It's just wasn't particularly helpful.

232
00:10:15,350 --> 00:10:18,280
For what it's worth, my mother says that when we deceive

233
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:21,020
for personal gain, we make jesue cry.

234
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:33,750
All right, what if we use this two-inch pvc

235
00:10:33,810 --> 00:10:35,310
To reinforce the center cross-support?

236
00:10:35,380 --> 00:10:36,710
No good.

237
00:10:36,780 --> 00:10:38,450
I mean, it might work for the japanese

238
00:10:38,510 --> 00:10:40,480
And the americans, but have you seen the size

239
00:10:40,550 --> 00:10:42,480
Of the russians they got up there?

240
00:10:44,410 --> 00:10:46,250
This thing has to hold up

241
00:10:46,310 --> 00:10:50,010
Against a hearty potato-based diet.

242
00:10:50,080 --> 00:10:52,350
I feel terrible.

243
00:10:52,410 --> 00:10:55,750
Maybe if you were helping, you'd feel better about yourself.

244
00:10:55,810 --> 00:11:00,350
I deliberately tried to sabotage stuart's date with penny.

245
00:11:00,410 --> 00:11:01,410
Of course you feel terrible.

246
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:04,080
You completely screwed up your karma, dude.

247
00:11:04,150 --> 00:11:05,950
You don't really believe in that superstition, do you?

248
00:11:06,010 --> 00:11:07,280
It's not superstition.

249
00:11:07,350 --> 00:11:08,880
It's practically newtonian.

250
00:11:08,950 --> 00:11:10,150
For every action,

251
00:11:10,210 --> 00:11:11,880
There's an equal and opposite reaction.

252
00:11:11,950 --> 00:11:13,550
Leonard pretends to be a friend

253
00:11:13,610 --> 00:11:14,980
And acts like a two-faced bitch.

254
00:11:17,810 --> 00:11:21,010
Therefore, he is reborn as a banana slug.

255
00:11:23,350 --> 00:11:25,180
It's actually a very elegant system.

256
00:11:25,250 --> 00:11:26,710
You know, what goes around comes around.

257
00:11:26,780 --> 00:11:30,310
Speaking of what goes around comes around...

258
00:11:30,380 --> 00:11:32,310
Okay, look.

259
00:11:32,380 --> 00:11:34,650
Instead of trying to reinforce this structure here,

260
00:11:34,710 --> 00:11:37,680
What if we just ran another line, bypass it entirely?

261
00:11:37,750 --> 00:11:40,380
It won't work. the diameter of the tubing is insufficient.

262
00:11:40,450 --> 00:11:42,410
What if we reposition the collection tank?

263
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:44,150
It won't work. no way to mount it.

264
00:11:44,210 --> 00:11:45,310
Okay, here's an idea.

265
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:46,910
What if I change my name and go live

266
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:49,480
With my cousin and her husband, avi, in israel?

267
00:11:51,450 --> 00:11:53,180
That could work.

268
00:11:59,310 --> 00:12:00,960
- Morning. morning. - what's up?

269
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:02,800
